<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.coding.sub-agent-live-claude</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>exec node "$@"</string>
        <string>node</string>
        <string>/Users/Q284340/Agentic/coding/scripts/sub-agent-live-claude.mjs</string>
        <string>--state-file</string>
        <string>/Users/Q284340/Agentic/coding/.data/sub-agent-live-state-claude.json</string>
    </array>
    <!-- KeepAlive: unconditional. Restart this daemon whenever it exits, for
         any reason. To stop one on purpose use `launchctl bootout` — never a
         kill, which is now indistinguishable from a crash.

         This was a <dict> of {SuccessfulExit=false, NetworkState=true} and both
         halves were wrong:

         * SuccessfulExit=false means "restart only on a NON-ZERO exit". These
           daemons trap SIGTERM, shut down gracefully and exit 0, so every
           signalled stop was permanent. On 2026-09-01 a stray pkill SIGTERMed
           all three; sub-agent capture stayed down 14.5 hours, reported by the
           Health API and acted on by nothing. Daemons with no graceful handler
           (auto-measure-foreground, prompt-classifier) took the same signal,
           exited non-zero, and launchd restarted them at once — the asymmetry
           was the SIGTERM handler, not the intent.

         * NetworkState=true looks like the safety net that covers the above.
           It is not: `man 5 launchd.plist` says it "is no longer implemented
           as it never acted how most users expected". So the dict had exactly
           one live condition, and dropping SuccessfulExit on its own left a
           dict that keeps the job alive under NO condition — verified on
           2026-09-02 by SIGTERMing the claude daemon and watching launchd
           leave it dead for three minutes. Hence plain <true/>, not a
           narrower dict. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/Q284340/Agentic/coding</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/Q284340/Agentic/coding/.data/live-claude.log</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/Q284340/Agentic/coding/.data/live-claude.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/sbin:/bin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
